%% P1 p.15 - sharding by aircraft registration: a booking is stored on the instance that owns the aircraft
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant I1 as instance1
    participant I2 as instance2 (owner of CS-TPC)
    participant DB2 as flightops-db-2

    C->>I1: POST /api/scheduled-flights {aircraft CS-TPC}
    Note over I1: owner of CS-TPC = highest SHA-256(name + "|CS-TPC")<br/>over instance1, instance2 -> instance2
    I1->>I2: POST /internal/flights (SERVICE JWT, not retried)
    I2->>DB2: lock aircraft CS-TPC (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE)
    I2->>DB2: overlapping flights of CS-TPC? none
    I2->>DB2: INSERT flight (route, aircraft, airports encrypted)
    DB2-->>I2: commit - lock released
    I2-->>I1: 201 flight
    I1-->>C: 201 flight, X-Instance: instance1, X-Stored-On: instance2
    Note over I1,I2: a 2nd booking of CS-TPC at the same moment (via either instance) waits for the lock,<br/>then sees this flight: 409 "already scheduled"
    Note over I1: owner unreachable (connection refused / circuit open): booked on instance1 instead (AP)<br/>owner reached but no answer in time: 503 "booking state unknown"
